                  <msItem>
                     <title source="3928">Florentius Wigornensis, etc.</title>
                  <title source="6762">Flor. Wigorniensis, etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes" source="6762">At fol. i (flyleaf): 'Md quod ff. Thomas
                        Straynsham deliberauit istum librum fratris Thome Powycke monacho maioris
                        maluernie et ipse deliberauit predicto Thome Straynsham librum uocatum Guido
                        de Bello Troiano anno dom. millesimo cccc octogesimo'. Straynsham was the
                        camerarius at Worcester, 1482--83.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="11XX" notBefore="1100" notAfter="1199" calendar="#gregorian">s. xii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#i" cert="low" source="3928"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_361">Great Malvern,
                        Worcestershire. Benedictine Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin and St Michael;
                        cell of Westminster</orgName><p>"Memorandum quod ffrater Thomas
                        S[tra]ynsham deliberauit istum librum ffratri Thome Powycke monachi
                        monasterii maioris Maluernie et ipse deliberauit predicto Thome Straynsham
                        librum vocatum Guido de bello Troiano" on flyleaf.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Originally at Worcester Cathedral, q.
                     v.</provenance>
               <provenance type="#c" source="6762"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_601">Worcester,
                        Worcestershire. Benedictine cathedral priory of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>There are Worcester marginal annals and flyleaf notes. In
                        addition, this manuscript contains writing in the same hand as appears in
                        Cambridge UL Kk.4.6 and Bodleian, Auct. F.1.9, which is probably that of
                        William of Worcester: for this hand see New Palaeographical Series, 2, pl.
                        87b.</p></provenance>
                  </history>
